WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.681
I want to invest in bonds. But where do I even begin?

2
00:00:03.952 --> 00:00:12.474
That question came up in our customer discovery: confusing bond
codes, unfamiliar platforms, and the feeling that you need a lot
of money.

3
00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:17.587
Meet In Creditble. Corporate bonds, explained one step at a
time.

4
00:00:17.858 --> 00:00:20.343
Built for your first bond. At your pace.

5
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.339
Let’s walk through a twenty five dollar demo investment.

6
00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:32.883
First, tell us how familiar you are with investing. New to
bonds? You get more explanation. Your risk comfort is a separate
choice.

7
00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:36.978
Start with your goals, not a bond identification code.

8
00:00:37.249 --> 00:00:47.275
Choose a target yield, how long you want to invest, and an
industry. A bank deposit benchmark gives you context, while the
risk information keeps the tradeoff visible.

9
00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:51.727
Instead of a wall of listings, explore three ranked matches.

10
00:00:51.998 --> 00:00:59.849
Each shows why it fits your choices, what the company does, and
what you should consider. Higher yield does not mean a safer
investment.

11
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.484
Still have a question? Ask for a little more help.

12
00:01:03.755 --> 00:01:13.098
The assistant explains terms and risks in plain English. In this
prototype, those answers are scripted examples, so you can test
the experience.

13
00:01:13.967 --> 00:01:17.264
When you choose buy, see the price before making a decision.

14
00:01:17.535 --> 00:01:25.227
The demo shows a price history and separate buying and selling
quotes. These are simulated prices, not live market data.

15
00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:30.355
You can start small. Fractional demo orders begin at ten
dollars.

16
00:01:30.625 --> 00:01:39.794
Here, twenty five dollars buys part of a bond. Review the final
cost, the bond amount, and estimated interest. Then confirm the
order yourself.

17
00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:45.476
The simulated order now appears in your holdings, and your
available cash updates.

18
00:01:45.747 --> 00:01:47.702
You can see exactly what changed.

19
00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:53.739
Back in your overview, switch from portfolio value to holdings
or upcoming payments.

20
00:01:54.010 --> 00:02:00.078
Sample connected accounts show the bigger picture, without
asking you to move your existing investments.

21
00:02:00.933 --> 00:02:05.700
More than ten customer discovery conversations helped shape this
prototype.

22
00:02:05.971 --> 00:02:14.218
Next, we’re testing whether first time investors understand the
choices, the risks, and the order. Your first bond. At your
pace.

23
00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:19.715
Contact our team on LinkedIn.
And special thanks to Pink Pan, our mentor.
